ootprint_type_mismatch. No claim is made that ignored checks pass.\n- Saved-board fill/connectivity only; no refill, fabrication output validation, physical measurement, detailed manufacturing or mechanical qualification.\n- Per explicit scope: no tolerances, ESR, leakage, parasitics, ratings, real part models, temperature, finite source impedance or external load evaluated.\n- Startup, reset, brownout, and other interface/operating cases are unspecified and not evaluated. This review establishes only the stated ideal shutdown case.\n\nConclusion: no evidence-supported circuit defect found within the specified scope.\nEOF\npython3 -c \\\"import json,pathlib; p=pathlib.Path('/work/experiments'); print((p/'shutdown.log').read_text()); print(json.dumps({k:json.loads((pathlib.Path('/evidence/checks')/(k+'.json')).read_text()).get('outcome') for k in ['erc','drc','netlist','geometry']})); print('Experiment files:', ', '.join(sorted(x.name for x in p.iterdir())))\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"\nNote: No compatibility mode selected!\n\n\nCircuit: ideal shutdown of native r1=10k and c1=100n\n\nDoing analysis at TEMP = 27.000000 and TNOM = 27.000000\n\nUsing transient initial conditions\n\nNo. of Data Rows : 6011\nvout_5ms            =  6.737944e-03\nt_10mv              =  4.605170e-03\nngspice-42 done\nUsing SPARSE 1.3 as Direct Linear Solver\n\n{\"erc\": \"pass\", \"drc\": \"pass\", \"netlist\": \"info\", \"geometry\": \"info\"}\nExperiment files: calculation.json, check_audit.json, commands.json, independent.xml, measurement.json, native_summary.json, notes.md, review.py, shutdown.cir, shutdown.log, shutdown_samples.dat\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
